.sp
The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates. Overrides config/env settings.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-read\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket read will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout\fP (int)
.sp
The maximum socket connect time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the socket connect will be blocking and not timeout. The default value is 60 seconds.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-binary\-format\fP (string)
.sp
The formatting style to be used for binary blobs. The default format is base64. The base64 format expects binary blobs to be provided as a base64 encoded string. The raw\-in\-base64\-out format preserves compatibility with AWS CLI V1 behavior and binary values must be passed literally. When providing contents from a file that map to a binary blob \fBfileb://\fP will always be treated as binary and use the file contents directly regardless of the \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP setting. When using \fBfile://\fP the file contents will need to properly formatted for the configured \fBcli\-binary\-format\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
base64
.IP \(bu 2
raw\-in\-base64\-out
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-pager\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable cli pager for output.
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.sp
\fB\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt\fP (boolean)
.sp
Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTo retrieve the inventory configuration for a bucket\fP
.sp
The following \fBget\-bucket\-inventory\-configuration\fP example retrieves the inventory configuration for the specified bucket with ID \fB1\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3api get\-bucket\-inventory\-configuration \e
    \-\-bucket amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket \e
    \-\-id 1
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{
    \(dqInventoryConfiguration\(dq: {
        \(dqIsEnabled\(dq: true,
        \(dqDestination\(dq: {
            \(dqS3BucketDestination\(dq: {
                \(dqFormat\(dq: \(dqORC\(dq,
                \(dqBucket\(dq: \(dqarn:aws:s3:::amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket\(dq,
                \(dqAccountId\(dq: \(dq123456789012\(dq
            }
        },
        \(dqIncludedObjectVersions\(dq: \(dqCurrent\(dq,
        \(dqId\(dq: \(dq1\(dq,
        \(dqSchedule\(dq: {
            \(dqFrequency\(dq: \(dqWeekly\(dq
        }
    }
}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
InventoryConfiguration \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the inventory configuration.
.sp
Destination \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Contains information about where to publish the inventory results.
.sp
S3BucketDestination \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Contains the bucket name, file format, bucket owner (optional), and prefix (optional) where inventory results are published.
.sp
AccountId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account ID that owns the destination S3 bucket. If no account ID is provided, the owner is not validated before exporting data.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Although this value is optional, we strongly recommend that you set it to help prevent problems if the destination bucket ownership changes.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Bucket \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the bucket where inventory results will be published.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Format \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the output format of the inventory results.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCSV\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBORC\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBParquet\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The prefix that is prepended to all inventory results.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Encryption \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Contains the type of server\-side encryption used to encrypt the inventory results.
.sp
SSES3 \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the use of SSE\-S3 to encrypt delivered inventory reports.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
SSEKMS \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the use of SSE\-KMS to encrypt delivered inventory reports.
.sp
KeyId \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the ID of the Key Management Service (KMS) symmetric encryption customer managed key to use for encrypting inventory reports.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IsEnabled \-> (boolean) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the inventory is enabled or disabled. If set to \fBTrue\fP , an inventory list is generated. If set to \fBFalse\fP , no inventory list is generated.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Filter \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies an inventory filter. The inventory only includes objects that meet the filter\(aqs criteria.
.sp
Prefix \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The prefix that an object must have to be included in the inventory results.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Id \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The ID used to identify the inventory configuration.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IncludedObjectVersions \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object versions to include in the inventory list. If set to \fBAll\fP , the list includes all the object versions, which adds the version\-related fields \fBVersionId\fP , \fBIsLatest\fP , and \fBDeleteMarker\fP to the list. If set to \fBCurrent\fP , the list does not contain these version\-related fields.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAll\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCurrent\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
OptionalFields \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Contains the optional fields that are included in the inventory results.
.sp
(string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSize\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLastModifiedDate\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStorageClass\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBETag\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIsMultipartUploaded\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBReplicationStatus\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEncryptionStatus\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBObjectLockRetainUntilDate\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBObjectLockMode\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBObjectLockLegalHoldStatus\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIntelligentTieringAccessTier\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBucketKeyStatus\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBChecksumAlgorithm\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBObjectAccessControlList\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBObjectOwner\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Schedule \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the schedule for generating inventory results.
.sp
Frequency \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies how frequently inventory results are produced.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDaily\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWeekly\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
